                        </div>
                        <ul>
                            <li>
                                <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i> <b>Front-End Development (Client-Side):</b> This layer focuses on building the user interface and ensuring a responsive user experience.
                                    <div class="mb-3" style="padding-left:2%">
                                    <b>Web Basics</b>: HTML5 (Semantic tags, Forms, Media) and CSS3 (Flexbox, Grid, Animations).
                                    </div>
                                <div class="mb-3" style="padding-left:2%">
                                    <b>Responsive Frameworks</b>: Bootstrap 5 or Tailwind CSS for mobile-first layouts.
                                </div>
                                <div class="mb-3" style="padding-left:2%">
                                    <b>JavaScript & TypeScript</b>: ES6+ syntax, DOM manipulation, and TypeScript for type-safe code.
                                </div>
                                <div class="mb-3" style="padding-left:2%">
                                    <b>Modern Frameworks</b>:  Angular (Modules, Components, RxJS) or React (Hooks, State, Props) are the most common industry choices
                                </div>

                            </li>
                            <li>
                                <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i> <b>Back-End Development (Server-Side):</b> This is the core "engine" of the application, typically built using the Microsoft ecosystem.
                                <div class="mb-3" style="padding-left:2%">
                                    <b>C# Language Fundamentals</b>: Variables, data types, control flow, and deep dive into Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) principles.
                                </div>
                                <div class="mb-3" style="padding-left:2%">
                                    <b>ASP.NET Core</b>: Building web applications using MVC (Model-View-Controller) architecture and Minimal APIs.
                                </div>
                                <div class="mb-3" style="padding-left:2%">
                                    <b>Web API</b>: Designing and securing RESTful services with JWT (JSON Web Tokens) and OAuth2.
                                </div>
                                <div class="mb-3" style="padding-left:2%">
                                    <b>ORM (Entity Framework Core)</b>: Database-first and code-first approaches, migrations, and LINQ queries.
                                </div>

                            </li>
                            <li>
                                <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i> <b>
                                    Database Management:
                                </b> Developers must manage data persistence and retrieval efficiently.
